 "notes": [
  "close_time is the API's `close_time` field. For markets that can close early and did, Kalshi rewrites it to the actual close; no field keeps the original schedule, so the entry candle is placed against the realized close.",
  "Window and split in UTC: 2021-07-01T00:00Z <= close_time < 2026-10-30T00:00Z; in-sample close_time < 2025-05-01T00:00Z.",
  "Settled yes or no = result 'yes'/'no' and status 'finalized'/'settled'.",
  "Non-multivariate = listed with mve_filter=exclude and no mve_collection_ticker (nor a KXMVE ticker).",
  "Archived markets from /historical/markets; settled markets still in the live set from /markets?status=settled (/events?status=settled drops settled markets whose event still has open ones); /events?tickers= maps events to series.",
  "Sampling: int(SHA-1 hex digest of the UTF-8 event_ticker) mod k == 0, k = 1, 2, ... until the eligible markets kept are <= 60,000; counted before the fee-type drop.",
  "Entry candle: the last daily candle (they end at midnight New York time) with end_period_ts <= close_time - 24 h. The 7 candles for the volume rule are the entry candle and the 6 candles before it as the API returns them (the API skips some days, so the window can be longer than 7 days; counted in diagnostics).",
  "A market whose lifetime volume (volume_fp) is under 100 contracts can't have 100 in any 7 candles, so its candles weren't fetched and it is counted under volume (volume_market_total) ahead of the other entry filters; the trade set is the same as fetching them.",
  "Spread = yes_ask close - yes_bid close at the entry candle; a candle without a bid or ask is skipped as no_quote. Kalshi shows a missing bid as 0.00 and a missing ask as 1.00, which the favourite range excludes.",
  "Fees use each series' current fee_type and fee_multiplier (some series have 0.5 or 0); fee changes over time are not modelled. Series absent from /series are dropped and counted (series_missing).",
  "The bars' 'mean' is the mean return per contract over trades; the event-clustered mean is reported beside it (verdict_event_mean in the JSON). t is over event means, ddof 1.",
  "Buckets use the ask of each side on markets that passed the entry filters: [0.50, 0.70) can take both sides of one market; [0.70, 0.85), [0.85, 0.97]; the longshot side is any ask in (0, 0.30), the mirror of the favourite rule.",
  "Maker version: the same trades as K1 (side chosen by the ask rule), bought at that side's bid (YES: yes bid; NO: 1 - yes ask), no fee. Fills not knowable.",
  "72 h entry: the same rule and filters on the last candle ending >= 72 h before close_time."
 ],
